                "message": "Add sp-org-issues: an issue tracker kept as a vulpea-para area\n\nOne Org file, created as the vulpea-para area \"Issues\", holds issues\nfor the dotfiles and vulpea-mcp, one heading per repository. Issues use\nthe org-gtd keywords through a file-local #+todo: line and carry\nORG_GTD: Actions, so NEXT issues show in org-gtd-engage.\n\n- C-c c I captures an issue under a chosen repository\n- C-c o a i i / i b: issue board and issues with a branch\n- sp-org-issues-start adds a git worktree for the issue's branch\n  (from the yadm repo for the dotfiles) and opens Magit there\n- closing an issue offers to remove its worktree\n- Magit lists untracked files in yadm worktrees\n\nLiterate source in docs/tangles/sp-org-issues.org; it tangles back to\nthe .el byte for byte. Loaded from init.el after sp-org-ext.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0171DJqqHwkZapaFawFrrrAN",
